# Changelog

All notable changes to Nexus Code are documented in this file.
The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/),
and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).

Detailed per-release documentation is maintained in [`docs/releases/`](docs/releases/).

## [Unreleased]

### Security

- Commands run through `run_command` no longer inherit credentials from the Nexus process. Variables from `~/.config/nexus/config.env`, plus anything named like a key, token, secret or password, `AWS_*`, `GH_TOKEN` and similar, are removed from the command environment, including inside the write-mod
- `--sandbox` now actually confines. Write-mode sandboxed commands run with `$HOME` masked, so `~/.ssh`, `~/.aws`, `~/.gnupg` and `~/.config/nexus` are unreadable, even when the workspace is, contains, or sits above `$HOME`. Only toolchain directories (`~/.cargo`, `~/.rustup`, `~/.nvm`, `~/.local/bi
- The legacy task-worktree merge refuses a worktree whose `.git` was replaced, and runs Git with hooks and fsmonitor disabled; a planted `core.fsmonitor` or hook in an agent-writable worktree no longer runs code outside it. The repository's own hooks no longer fire on that commit and merge.
- The `--sandbox docker` engine runs a digest-pinned image (alpine 3.23) as the invoking uid with all capabilities dropped, `no-new-privileges`, a read-only root plus a tmpfs `/tmp`, a 512-process limit, and no network unless `--sandbox-network` / `NEXUS_SANDBOX_NETWORK=1` is set. Only the scrubbed 
- A compaction summary (including `compact --llm`) is now labelled in every request as untrusted data with its source, under the "Structured Context Memory" header: text from earlier tool output or fetched pages that reached the summary is information about the task, never instructions. The label is
- Prompt-injection scanner (CS-7): a tool result that carries instruction-like text aimed at the assistant, hidden or bidirectional Unicode, fake chat or tool-call markup, or an encoded payload of those is labelled and fenced (`<<<UNTRUSTED RESULT BEGIN/END>>>`, content kept, hidden characters shown

### Changed

- The dependency deprecation check retries a transient npm registry failure (network error, timeout, truncated body, HTTP 429 or 5xx) up to 3 times, 1 s then 3 s apart, before failing closed; a 404 or 403 is a real answer and is not retried. A single registry blip had turned main red.
